title:: CaosBox
summary:: High-level CaosBox facade: startup, transport, routing and palette.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosGear, Classes/CaosSequencer, Classes/CaosEngine, Classes/CaosBoxGUI

description::
CaosBox is the application facade. It creates the link::Classes/CaosEngine::, loads
the startup files and exposes transport, BPM, step duration, per-track routing and
the analyzers.

The public API is preserved from previous versions: code::CaosBox.play::,
code::CaosBox.stop::, code::CaosBox.bpm(140)::, and so on can still be used.

classmethods::

subsection:: Startup

method:: environment
Starts the engine and loads the SynthDefs, instruments and GUI.
code::
CaosBox.environment;        // with GUI
CaosBox.environment(false); // without opening the window
::

method:: close
Stops the sequencer, frees the engine and disconnects the MIDI mapping.

subsection:: Transport

method:: play
method:: pause
method:: stop
code::play:: starts or resumes from the current step; code::pause:: keeps the step;
code::stop:: returns to step 0 for the next play.

method:: bpm
code::
CaosBox.bpm(126);
::

method:: stepDur
Duration of one step in beats. code::0.25:: = Fourths, code::1/3:: = Thirds.
code::
CaosBox.stepDur(1/3);
::

method:: randomTime
Enables randomized timing per step.
code::
CaosBox.randomTime(true);
CaosBox.randomTime(false);
::

subsection:: Routing

method:: route
Routes a melodic track to an engine bus. Accepts a name, an index or a
link::Classes/Bus::. Without an argument it returns the current route.
code::
CaosBox.route(\bass, \reverb);
CaosBox.route(\bass, 52);
CaosBox.route(\bass);
::

subsection:: Pattern generation

method:: randPattern
Replaces the gates of one track with a new random pattern. code::density:: is the
probability (0..1) that each step is on. Without code::every:: it is a one-shot
change; with code::every: n:: it is applied again every code::n:: full loops of
the link::Classes/CaosSequencer:: (code::size:: steps). The first pattern is
applied immediately.
code::
CaosBox.randPattern(\kick, density: 0.5);
CaosBox.randPattern(\kick, density: 0.25, every: 4);
::
Only the gates change: on melodic tracks the notes, chords and voice sequences
are untouched. On percussion tracks the whole pattern is replaced, so its flams
are cleared too. Before changing the track, the current gates and flams are saved
as a one-level history for code::restorePattern::. Periodic regenerations do not
overwrite that saved pattern. A one-shot call does not cancel an evolution
already running; use code::stopRandPattern:: for that. A manual random pattern
also cancels an active code::fill::, using the fill base as its history. Returns
the link::Classes/CaosTrack::. The old code::randSteps:: remains available for an
exact number of steps.

method:: stopRandPattern
Stops the periodic regeneration of a track. The current pattern stays as it is.
code::
CaosBox.stopRandPattern(\kick);
::

method:: restorePattern
Restores the gates and flams that were on the track immediately before the last
code::randPattern:: call. It is a one-level undo: the history is consumed and the
periodic evolution, if any, is stopped so the next loop cannot overwrite the
restored pattern. It also cancels an active code::fill::. Returns the
link::Classes/CaosTrack::.
code::
CaosBox.randPattern(\kick, density: 0.25);
CaosBox.restorePattern(\kick);
::

method:: fill
Applies a temporary random pattern and restores the gates and flams that were
there when code::fill:: was called, after code::loops:: complete loops of the
sequencer. The default is one loop. If it is called halfway through a loop, that
partial loop is finished first and then the complete loops are counted.
code::
CaosBox.fill(\kick, density: 0.75);
CaosBox.fill(\kick, density: 0.75, loops: 2);
::
code::fill:: applies the random pattern immediately. It stops a periodic
code::randPattern:: so the evolution cannot overwrite the fill, and only one fill
can be active per track. code::restorePattern:: ends it early; otherwise the
base pattern returns automatically. Returns the link::Classes/CaosTrack::. If
the sequencer is not running, the fill stays until it starts looping or until
code::restorePattern:: is called.

subsection:: Mute and solo

method:: mute
Silences one track without clearing it or stopping its sequencer. The pattern is
kept and a muted melodic line keeps advancing, but it does not trigger. A note
that is already sounding is not cut; mute acts on the next trigger. Returns the
new state.
code::
CaosBox.mute(\kick, true);
CaosBox.mute(\kick, false);
::

method:: solo
Makes one track the only audible one. Several tracks can be soloed at the same
time. A muted track stays silent even when soloed (mute wins). As with mute, a
note already sounding is not cut; solo acts on the next trigger. Returns the new
state.
code::
CaosBox.solo(\bass, true);   // only the soloed tracks are heard
CaosBox.solo(\bass, false);  // back to the full mix
::

subsection:: Analyzers and GUI

method:: freqAnalyzer
Opens or closes the floating FFT and oscilloscope window.
code::
CaosBox.freqAnalyzer(true);
CaosBox.freqAnalyzer(false);
::

method:: gui
Returns the link::Classes/CaosBoxGUI:: registry.
code::
CaosBox.gui.color(\orange);
CaosBox.gui.color([0.2, 0.6, 1.0]);
::
